{"id": "2026-11-23-news-cop31-ends-with-no-climate-decision", "date": "2026-11-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "COP31 ends with no climate decision", "summary": "The COP31 climate summit in Antalya ended on Sunday 22 November without adopting a final decision, after a broad coalition including Switzerland, the EU and climate-vulnerable countries rejected a text that contained no recommendation to move away from fossil fuels.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/-P0GlW8Lcfw2", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["geopolitics", "switzerland"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "The COP31 climate summit in Antalya ended on Sunday 22 November without adopting a final decision, after a broad coalition including Switzerland, the EU and climate-vulnerable countries rejected a text that contained no recommendation to move away from fossil fuels. \"I understand that there is no agreement on this text. For that reason, these decisions have not been adopted,\" COP president Murat Kurum, Türkiye's environment minister, said after two weeks of talks and two days of overtime; UN News says Antalya is now the longest-running UN climate summit on record. The Swiss environment department's statement says oil-producing countries \"led by Saudi Arabia\" blocked any fossil-fuel language, so the coalition voted the draft down even though Switzerland backed its headline goal of raising electricity to 35% of global final energy use by 2035. UN Secretary-General António Guterres called the outcome \"deeply disappointing\" and said: \"There may be no consensus in the negotiating room. There is no ambiguity in the science.\" Federal Councillor Albert Rösti presented Switzerland's roadmap for leaving fossil fuels and announced, subject to parliament's approval, CHF 132.1 million for the Global Environment Facility and CHF 29.33 million for two climate funds aimed at the poorest and most exposed countries.", "why": "with no decision at all, the 2023 Dubai pledge to \"transition away\" from fossil fuels stays the furthest the UN process has gone, and Switzerland says it will keep working from that text instead.", "thread_id": "2026-11-23-news-cop31-ends-with-no-climate-decision", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-23", "event_date": "2026-11-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["COP31", "Saudi Arabia", "Albert Rösti", "António Guterres"]}
{"id": "2026-11-23-news-ukraine-says-it-sank-russian-corvette-off-libya", "date": "2026-11-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Ukraine says it sank Russian corvette off Libya", "summary": "President Volodymyr Zelensky said on Monday 23 November that Ukraine sank the Russian navy corvette Merkury in the port of Benghazi, eastern Libya, and hit a Russian cargo ship off the Libyan coast, in attacks with seven Ukrainian-built naval drones on Sunday 22 November.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/23/zelenskyy-says-ukraine-behind-drone-attacks-on-russian-ships-near-libya", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "President Volodymyr Zelensky said on Monday 23 November that Ukraine sank the Russian navy corvette Merkury in the port of Benghazi, eastern Libya, and hit a Russian cargo ship off the Libyan coast, in attacks with seven Ukrainian-built naval drones on Sunday 22 November. Zelensky called the Merkury one of Russia's newest warships, said a Ka-27 military helicopter was also destroyed, and said the cargo ship, which he named as the Angara, carries weapons for Russia. Libyan media and naval analysts say the cargo ship hit was the Ascalon, a near-identical vessel, so it is not yet clear whether one or two freighters were struck. Eastern Libya's authorities said the corvette had docked to refuel and resupply on its way back to Russia, that about ten people were injured, and that more than 20 drone boats were intercepted off Benghazi; satellite images show only the bow still above water. Saddam Haftar, deputy commander of the eastern forces, said Libya rejects being used \"as an arena for settling scores\", and the UN mission in Libya (UNSMIL) called for \"an immediate, independent and transparent investigation\". Russia had not commented officially by Monday morning.", "why": "a day after a Russian freighter was set on fire in the Gulf of Finland, Ukraine says it is now striking Russian ships on the far side of the Mediterranean, in the port of a country that is not a party to the war.", "thread_id": "2026-11-23-news-ukraine-says-it-sank-russian-corvette-off-libya", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-23", "event_date": "2026-11-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Ukraine", "Russia", "Libya", "Merkury", "UNSMIL"]}
{"id": "2026-11-23-news-dymer-strike-toll-rises-to-11", "date": "2026-11-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Dymer strike toll rises to 11", "summary": "The death toll from the Russian drone strike on a five-storey apartment block in Dymer, north of Kyiv, rose to at least 11 on Monday 23 November, and Russian attacks across the Kyiv region killed at least 15 people.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/23/death-toll-rises-after-deadly-russian-attacks-on-ukraine", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The death toll from the Russian drone strike on a five-storey apartment block in Dymer, north of Kyiv, rose to at least 11 on Monday 23 November, and Russian attacks across the Kyiv region killed at least 15 people. Kyiv regional official Tymur Tkachenko said rescuers pulled another body from the rubble, and the State Emergency Service said 11 people, including two children, were still unaccounted for. A strike on a supermarket in Vyshneve, just south of the capital, killed three people and wounded 15, including three children, and a strike on a house in Bila Tserkva killed one.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-23-news-dymer-strike-toll-rises-to-11", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-23", "event_date": "2026-11-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Ukraine", "Russia", "Dymer", "Kyiv"]}
{"id": "2026-11-23-news-democrats-reach-258-house-seats", "date": "2026-11-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Democrats reach 258 House seats", "summary": "Democrats will hold 258 of the 435 seats in the next US House of Representatives, the largest majority either party has held since 1992, after Chuck Hubbard beat Republican incumbent Virginia Foxx in North Carolina in one of the last undecided races of the 3 November midterms, CBS News and NBC projected on Sunday 22 November.", "url": "https://www.lemonde.fr/international/article/2026/11/23/avec-258-sieges-remportes-les-democrates-decrochent-la-plus-large-majorite-depuis-1992-a-la-chambre-des-representants_6814364_3210.html", "source_domain": "lemonde.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Democrats will hold 258 of the 435 seats in the next US House of Representatives, the largest majority either party has held since 1992, after Chuck Hubbard beat Republican incumbent Virginia Foxx in North Carolina in one of the last undecided races of the 3 November midterms, CBS News and NBC projected on Sunday 22 November. The result came after a recount. Democratic leader Hakeem Jeffries, set to become Speaker when the new House sits in early January, would be the first African American in the post.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-23-news-democrats-reach-258-house-seats", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-23", "event_date": "2026-11-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["US House of Representatives", "Hakeem Jeffries", "Democratic Party"]}
{"id": "2026-11-23-news-drones-hit-un-building-in-khartoum", "date": "2026-11-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Drones hit UN building in Khartoum", "summary": "Drones struck a residential area of Khartoum overnight into Sunday 22 November and damaged a UN building in a civilian neighbourhood, the UN's humanitarian office (OCHA) said.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/sudan-drones-hit-un-building-residential-area-in-khartoum/a-80015122", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Drones struck a residential area of Khartoum overnight into Sunday 22 November and damaged a UN building in a civilian neighbourhood, the UN's humanitarian office (OCHA) said. \"It is unacceptable that we are put at such risk,\" said Denise Brown, the UN's humanitarian coordinator for Sudan. AFP reported explosions around Khartoum airport and elsewhere in the city between about 2:00 and 4:30 a.m.; there were no immediate reports of casualties. A Sudanese army source said the drones were launched from Ethiopia, which has denied similar accusations before. The UN says drones killed more than 1,100 people in Sudan's war in the first six months of this year.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-23-news-drones-hit-un-building-in-khartoum", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-23", "event_date": "2026-11-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Sudan", "Khartoum", "OCHA", "Ethiopia"]}
{"id": "2026-11-23-news-istanbul-marches-against-media-takeovers", "date": "2026-11-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Istanbul marches against media takeovers", "summary": "Several thousand people marched through Istanbul on Sunday 22 November against the closure of opposition-aligned media, days after police raided Sozcu TV, arrested senior staff and placed the channel under a government-appointed trustee.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-thousands-protest-closure-of-critical-media-outlets/a-80015347", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Several thousand people marched through Istanbul on Sunday 22 November against the closure of opposition-aligned media, days after police raided Sozcu TV, arrested senior staff and placed the channel under a government-appointed trustee. DW reports that it is the third such takeover in a year, after Tele1 and Halk TV, and that the protest was called by the opposition party Yeni Parti. The media rights group MLSA counts 25 journalists in prison in Turkey, and Reporters Without Borders ranks the country 163rd of 180 for press freedom.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-23-news-istanbul-marches-against-media-takeovers", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-23", "event_date": "2026-11-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Turkey", "Sozcu TV", "Istanbul"]}
{"id": "2026-11-23-news-houthis-report-deaths-in-hodeida-strikes", "date": "2026-11-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Houthis report deaths in Hodeida strikes", "summary": "The Houthis' Al-Masirah TV said on Monday 23 November that Saudi strikes on a state telecoms company building in the Yemeni port of Hodeida killed 10 people and wounded more than 20, figures AFP could not verify.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/monde/moyenorient/en-direct-moyen-orient-des-frappes-saoudiennes-visent-le-port-d-hodeida-selon-un-media-houthis", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source", "disputed"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The Houthis' Al-Masirah TV said on Monday 23 November that Saudi strikes on a state telecoms company building in the Yemeni port of Hodeida killed 10 people and wounded more than 20, figures AFP could not verify. The channel first reported four dead. The Saudi-led coalition backing Yemen's internationally recognised government had claimed strikes on Friday 20 November on Hodeida sites it says are used for smuggling weapons and ballistic missiles, as the Houthis advance towards Aden.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-23-news-houthis-report-deaths-in-hodeida-strikes", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-23", "event_date": "2026-11-23", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Houthis", "Saudi Arabia", "Hodeida", "Yemen"]}
{"id": "2026-11-23-news-trial-of-vaud-mp-buffat-opens", "date": "2026-11-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Trial of Vaud MP Buffat opens", "summary": "The trial of Vaud SVP national councillor Michaël Buffat, accused of domestic violence against his ex-wife between 2015 and 2024, opened before a Vaud criminal court on Monday 23 November.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/schweiz/svp-nationalrat-vor-gericht-michael-buffat-wollte-kommandieren-kontrollieren-korrigieren", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The trial of Vaud SVP national councillor Michaël Buffat, accused of domestic violence against his ex-wife between 2015 and 2024, opened before a Vaud criminal court on Monday 23 November. According to the indictment, he repeatedly threatened her with death, locked her in, tracked her phone, and once pointed a gun at her and asked what she would do \"if I kill you now\"; several weapons were seized. The prosecutor lists simple bodily harm, false imprisonment, abduction and coercion, which carry up to three years in prison. Buffat has filed a counter-complaint for extortion, and his ex-wife is also a defendant: she is accused of coercion over a divorce settlement in which he paid CHF 100,000 in exchange for her silence, of recording conversations without consent and of simple bodily harm. Buffat has not commented and is presumed innocent; he has stepped back from the Vaud party leadership and resigned from the board of the cantonal fire and natural-hazards insurer. The Vaud SVP says he must give up all his offices if convicted. About ten women demonstrated outside in support of the complainant.", "why": "a sitting member of the National Council from Vaud is on trial for domestic violence, and a 2015 complaint by an earlier partner was never examined because deadlines were missed.", "thread_id": "2026-11-23-news-trial-of-vaud-mp-buffat-opens", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-23", "event_date": "2026-11-23", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Michaël Buffat", "SVP Vaud", "Vaud"]}
{"id": "2026-11-23-news-swiss-home-care-hits-record-hours", "date": "2026-11-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss home care hits record hours", "summary": "Home-care services in Switzerland delivered a record 29.6 million hours of care in 2025, 15.3% more than in 2024, and hospital outpatient billing passed CHF 10 billion for the first time, the Federal Statistical Office (FSO) said on Monday 23 November.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/xsLqZQ654tIy", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland", "health"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Home-care services in Switzerland delivered a record 29.6 million hours of care in 2025, 15.3% more than in 2024, and hospital outpatient billing passed CHF 10 billion for the first time, the Federal Statistical Office (FSO) said on Monday 23 November. Hospital outpatient contacts rose 3.9%, while inpatient stays grew only 1.8% and nursing-home places 0.9%. Most of the home-care growth came from for-profit companies: 227 new ones opened in 2025, bringing the total to 1,050 (+24.4%), and their hours rose 37.6% to 12.2 million. For the first time the FSO counted family carers hired and paid by these services: 43% of for-profit firms and 20% of public non-profit organisations employ them.", "why": "care is moving out of hospital beds and into homes and outpatient clinics, and that shift is where much of the growth behind compulsory health-insurance premiums is coming from.", "thread_id": "2026-11-23-news-swiss-home-care-hits-record-hours", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-23", "event_date": "2026-11-23", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Statistical Office"]}
{"id": "2026-11-23-news-army-to-guard-osce-meeting-in-lugano", "date": "2026-11-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Army to guard OSCE meeting in Lugano", "summary": "Up to 2,000 Swiss soldiers will support Ticino police in securing the 33rd OSCE Ministerial Council in Lugano on Thursday 3 and Friday 4 December, the defence department said on Monday 23 November.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/SLfi0iF0vhyH", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Up to 2,000 Swiss soldiers will support Ticino police in securing the 33rd OSCE Ministerial Council in Lugano on Thursday 3 and Friday 4 December, the defence department said on Monday 23 November. The army will guard sites, run air surveillance, provide transport and logistics, and patrol Lake Lugano by boat, and airspace over Lugano will be restricted during the meeting. The Federal Council approved the deployment on 18 September.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-23-news-army-to-guard-osce-meeting-in-lugano", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-23", "event_date": "2026-12-03", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["OSCE", "Swiss Army", "Lugano", "Ticino"]}
